  "data": {
    "body": "The homogeneous differential equation \\[y''-\\frac{3}{x}y'+\\frac{4}{x^2}y=0, \\textrm{  }x>0\\] has two solutions $y_1(x)=x^2$ and $y_2(x)=x^2\\ln{(x)}$. Use the method of variation of parameters to find a particular solution of the nonhomogeneous differential equation \\[y''-\\frac{3}{x}y'+\\frac{4}{x^2}y=2,\\textrm{  }x>0\\]",
    "solution": "\\[\ny_p = x^2 (\\ln{x})^2\n\\]",
